# ui.rules — screens, widgets, tokens, strings
# SOP: sop/ui-architecture.md
# Guardrails: guardrails/ui.md

## Boundaries
MUST-NOT  UI-1   Call container lookups ($LOOKUP), repositories, data sources, the gateway, or storage ($STORAGE) from a widget; take values from state or constructor params.
MUST-NOT  UI-2   Put network calls, storage access, decryption, heavy computation or business rules in build/initState/didChangeDependencies.
MUST      ARCH-5 Move filtering/sorting/validation/threshold checks into the Cubit or a policy; the widget dispatches intent and renders state.
MUST-NOT  UI-14  Use a global BuildContext (static appContext / navigatorKey.currentContext) for sizing/theming; use the local context.

## Screens
MUST      UI-15  Screen = routed XScreen (StatelessWidget unless it owns controllers/observers) whose route/screen wrapper provides its state holder; initial load at that wrapper (..load()) or initState.
MUST      UI-6   Render loading, error (with retry), empty and no-internet states for every data-driven screen.
MUST      UI-7   One loader style per state: blocking overlay loader from a listener OR inline loader widget from the builder — never both.
MUST      STATE-12 Keep navigation/toast/dialog/loader side effects in BlocListener (with listenWhen), not in build.
SHOULD    UI-16  Use a shared state-render widget (loading/error/empty/content) instead of repeating status if-chains.

## Widgets
MUST      UI-4   Search core/widgets, presentation/commonWidgets and presentation/shared before creating a widget; never add a duplicate button, text field, loader, toast, sheet helper, avatar or network-image wrapper.
SHOULD    UI-17  Extract a widget when reused in 2+ places, when it has local state, when build > ~100 lines, or when it needs its own BlocSelector. Don't fragment single-use 10-line pieces into files.
SHOULD    UI-18  Prefer private widget classes over builder methods for rebuild scoping.
MUST      UI-11  Dispose TextEditingController/ScrollController/AnimationController/FocusNode and remove observers/listeners in dispose().
SHOULD    UI-9   Keep files < 400 lines, build < 100 lines, and <= ~8 BlocProviders per screen wrapper.
MUST-NOT  UI-10  Keep fully commented-out widgets/screens in the tree.
MUST-NOT  UI-12  Use Future.delayed to wait for a router/cubit/plugin; intentional UX delays use a named constant + comment.
SHOULD    UI-19  Avoid My/Custom prefixes for new widgets; use descriptive nouns (AppButton, PrimaryButton, UserAvatar).

## Design tokens
MUST      UI-3   Use the project design tokens (PR-F1: colors, spacing, radii, typography). No new Colors.* (except transparent), Color(0x...), fontSize:, inline TextStyle(...) or magic EdgeInsets in feature code.
MUST      UI-20  Keep the one theme stack recorded in PR-F1. Inspect actual usage; never delete or adopt theme classes based on historical reference-app names.

## Strings
MUST      UI-5   Take user-facing strings from the PR-F2 string source (l10n or constants); never Text('literal') in feature code.
DECISION  ND-5   Localization approach per docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md (l10n .arb vs constants class); ask if _TBD_.

## Lists, images, forms
MUST      UI-8   Use ListView.builder/SliverList for server lists; paginate; stable ValueKey(id) for items with state.
MUST      UI-13  Load network images through the project image wrapper(s); no raw Image.network or unwrapped CachedNetworkImage; set cache sizes for large images.
SHOULD    UI-21  New forms: Cubit-side validation exposing fieldErrors in state; regexes from RegExpressions. Do not add toast-only validation.
MUST      UI-22  Show sheets/dialogs via the project's sheet/dialog helpers (showXSheet/showXDialog); sheet content is a widget class when > 30 lines.

## Responsive
SHOULD    UI-23  Branch on breakpoints only when layouts differ; do not wrap screens in a responsive wrapper that returns the same widget for every size.
MUST      UI-27  Read colors from the theme/ColorScheme/ThemeExtension; every screen readable in light and dark (if dark is supported). (sop/theming-and-responsive.md)
MUST-NOT  UI-28  Hardcode screen-wide widths/heights; use constraints, LayoutBuilder and the breakpoint tokens; respect SafeArea and keyboard insets.
MUST-NOT  UI-29  Write asset path strings ('assets/...') in widgets; use the generated asset class or asset constants.

## Forms (sop/forms-and-validation.md)
MUST      UI-24  Put validation rules in the state holder or pure validators; widgets render field errors from state, mapped to l10n.
MUST      UI-25  Set keyboardType/textInputAction/autofillHints; disable or show progress on submit while in flight; ignore re-submits in the state holder.
MUST      UI-26  Sensitive fields: obscureText, enableSuggestions:false, autocorrect:false; never logged; cleared from state after submit.

## Project
PROJECT   See docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md for overrides and open decisions.
MUST-NOT  Invent class/file names from profiles/reference/ or example ADRs when docs/project/flutter/ still has _TBD_ stubs.
